WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.310
Meet one thousand dollars.

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:07.210
Let's see what happens if we just leave it alone and let it grow.

3
00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:10.733
Say it earns eight percent a year.

4
00:00:10.733 --> 00:00:17.446
That's a bit below what the US stock market has averaged over long periods in the past.

5
00:00:17.446 --> 00:00:20.069
Real years go up and down, though.

6
00:00:20.969 --> 00:00:24.345
After one year, you earn eighty dollars.

7
00:00:24.345 --> 00:00:27.468
Now you have one thousand and eighty.

8
00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:29.786
Here's the magic.

9
00:00:29.786 --> 00:00:35.871
In year two, you earn eight percent on the whole one thousand and eighty,

10
00:00:35.871 --> 00:00:38.288
including last year's growth.

11
00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:40.622
That's interest on interest.

12
00:00:40.622 --> 00:00:42.623
It's called compounding.

13
00:00:43.523 --> 00:00:49.395
After ten years, you have about two thousand one hundred sixty dollars.

14
00:00:49.395 --> 00:00:51.298
Your money has doubled.

15
00:00:52.198 --> 00:00:57.534
Keep going to thirty years, and you have about ten thousand dollars.

16
00:00:57.534 --> 00:01:01.537
Ten times your money, without adding a single cent.

17
00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:07.503
Without compounding, earning eight percent on just the original thousand,

18
00:01:07.503 --> 00:01:10.556
you'd have only three thousand four hundred.

19
00:01:11.457 --> 00:01:13.593
The secret ingredient is time.

20
00:01:13.593 --> 00:01:19.431
Starting ten years earlier can make a bigger difference than investing more later.

21
00:01:20.331 --> 00:01:21.626
But watch out.

22
00:01:21.626 --> 00:01:25.787
Compounding works against you with debt, too.

23
00:01:25.787 --> 00:01:29.486
Credit card interest grows the same way.

24
00:01:30.386 --> 00:01:35.947
So start early, be patient, and let time do the heavy lifting.

25
00:01:35.947 --> 00:01:39.805
This is for learning, not financial advice.

